n_id":"tx-hhsc-122554-i20240403","date":"2024-04-03","original_code":"746.2805","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-05-14","finding":"Prohibited Punishments - No Harsh, Cruel or Unusual: A caregiver repeatedly hit a child in the face (e.g., 5 times) with his own hand along with requiring him to face the outside wall, and the caregiver wrapped the child?s arm around his own neck as well.  The caregiver inappropriately picked another child up by her arm, shoulders and her hair to get her to sit against a wall outside.  The caregiver threw a shoe at a child, and the caregiver put the child?s shoe in the garbage can as well.","topic":"sanitation","source_record_id":"1026673243","violation_type_title":"Prohibited Punishments - No Harsh, Cruel or Unusual (26 TAC §746.2805)","topic_label":"Sanitation & hygiene"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-122554-i20240403-v2","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-4","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-122554-i20240403","date":"2024-04-03","original_code":"746.1201(4)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-05-14","finding":"AP Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Ensure No Child Abused, Neglected, or Exploited: DFPS staff determined there was reason to believe that a caregiver physically abused two children in care during a disciplinary incident at the facility.","topic":"staffing","source_record_id":"1026668665","violation_type_title":"AP Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Ensure No Child Abused, Neglected, or Exploited (26 TAC §746.1201(4))","topic_label":"Staff qualifications & clearances"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-122554-i20240403-v3","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1201-1","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-122554-i20240403","date":"2024-04-03","original_code":"746.1201(1)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-05-14","finding":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control: Rather than calming herself and removing herself from the situation upon admittedly becoming overwhelmed, a caregiver persisted in her aggression, leading to the maltreatment/abuse of two children in care.  Another caregiver exhibited poor judgment when she failed to intervene appropriately (e.g., by failing to alert other operation staff or verbally confronting her coworker for her abusive behaviors in the moment) during a disciplinary issue at the facility.","topic":"supervision","source_record_id":"1026667631","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Employees and Caregivers -Demonstrate Competency, Good Judgment, Self-control (26 TAC §746.1201(1))","topic_label":"Supervision & ratios"},{"id":"tx-hhsc-122554-i20240403-v4","violation_type_id":"tx-tac-746-1205-a-5","inspection_id":"tx-hhsc-122554-i20240403","date":"2024-04-03","original_code":"746.1205(a)(5)","severity":"high","severity_label":"High risk","status":"corrected","status_label":"Correction verified 2024-05-14","finding":"Responsibilities of Caregivers - Intervene to ensure each child's safety: A caregiver failed to intervene to prevent a child from hitting her head on concrete during a disciplinary incident at the facility.  The caregiver failed to separate the children and prevent them from hitting each other.  Another caregiver failed to appropriately intervene in response to the escalating aggression which led to the abuse of two children in care.","topic":"other","source_record_id":"1026662845","violation_type_title":"Responsibilities of Caregivers - Intervene to ensure each child's safety (26 TAC §746.1205(a)(5))","topic_label":"Other"}]},{"id":"tx-hhsc-122554-i20230912","date":"2023-09-12","inspection_type":"Inspection","result":"No deficiencies cited","passed":true,"violation_count":0,"open_count":0,"evidence_class":"VERIFIED","provenance":{"source_id":"tx_hhsc_activities","source_record_id":"905754538","url":"htt